<title>BELGIUM: Tractebel unit, Siemens in Russia contract.</title>
<headline>Tractebel unit, Siemens in Russia contract.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tractebel Engineering subsidiary  Belgatom said on Tuesday it had a 30 percent share in a 3.3 million Ecu (130 million Belgian franc) contract to supply training equipment to a Russian nuclear power station.</p>
<p>The European Union contract to supply simulation equipment to the Beloyarsk fast breeder reactor in Uralsk was awarded to a consortium also comprising German engineering group Siemens and  Corys, Tractebel said in a statement.</p>
<p>Siemens' share is 40 percent, a Tractebel spokesman said.</p>
